# Two opposite-bias branches executed in blocks of 5:
# 0x100 is always Taken, 0x200 is always Not Taken.
# At every block boundary the GHR holds the same value for both branches
# (all-1s after 0x100's block, all-0s after 0x200's block), so they train
# the same PHT counters in opposite directions: destructive aliasing.
# The low 4 bits of 0x100 and 0x200 are identical (both 0), so gshare's
# XOR-with-address maps them to the same indices and cannot help.
0x100 T
0x100 T
0x100 T
0x100 T
0x100 T
0x200 N
